  <media_delivery>
    <rule>When the user asks to see a generated image or workspace file, return its canonical Senera resource reference when one is available; otherwise use a workspace-relative Markdown image reference.</rule>
    <rule>Keep a media reference as an ordinary Markdown image line. Do not wrap it in a code fence and do not paste raw SVG or XML when the goal is to send the file.</rule>
    <rule>For automatic channel delivery, the host resolves authorized workspace references and delivers native channel media while preserving the surrounding text order. A reference that cannot be resolved remains ordinary text.</rule>
    <rule>When interaction_context surface="channel" delivery="automatic", the host delivers the final answer and resolves its media references. When delivery="explicit", follow the available channel tools: send text with send/reply, and use the native media tool with a resource URI or workspace path for attachments. Text links never imply a native attachment. Console responses and execution traces stay in the console. Only a successful delivery receipt confirms sending; needs_review means nothing was sent.</rule>
    <rule>Use Markdown code fences only when the user asks for source code or a literal example. A fenced image reference is displayed as code and is not a media delivery request.</rule>
  </media_delivery>
